WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-synthesis (90s) Narrator Joy

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.808
First, generating text from scratch for already-solved problems wastes electricity and invites avoidable mistakes.

2
00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:16.366
Second, an energy-ordered cascade checks microjoule lookup tables and exact verifiers first, waking large models last.

3
00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:24.853
Third, every accepted answer passes deterministic checks and crystallizes downward into a fast, reusable lookup skill.

4
00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:31.753
Across real software engineering and scientific computing, most daily requests repeat structural patterns

5
00:00:31.753 --> 00:00:37.544
already solved thousands of times before. Treating every single prompt like an unsolved mystery

6
00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:43.518
forces massive neural networks to burn heavy electrical power re-deriving known work from scratch.

7
00:00:44.018 --> 00:00:49.009
On synthesis dot openie dot dev, every task steps down an energy-ordered ladder.

8
00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:55.809
Microjoule lookup tables and exact deterministic solvers answer recurring patterns first; only genuine misses

9
00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:02.484
stream active slices of a thirty-five-billion-parameter model inside nine hundred seventy megabytes of RAM.

10
00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:08.661
Across open multi-library Python coding suites, this synthesis cascade solved ninety point six

11
00:01:08.661 --> 00:01:13.672
two percent of tasks and ninety-one point six seven percent of our forty-eight-task

12
00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:19.590
benchmark, while closing forty out of forty iterative repairs with zero broken repository commits.

13
00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.014
Whenever a new candidate patch passes deterministic test gates,

14
00:01:24.014 --> 00:01:30.927
it crystallizes downward into fast lookup memory so tomorrow's repeat request finishes cleanly in microseconds.
